You have refractive amblyopia. This means vision in one eye did not develop normally in childhood because that eye was consistently blurrier, often from a stronger prescription or a large difference between the two eyes.\
\
The eye itself can be healthy, but the visual system learned to rely more on the clearer eye during development. Because of that, the weaker eye may not see as well even with the correct glasses.\
